00:37:19.290 --> 00:37:25.350
So what is deep learning compared to the machine
learning and the tree based learning that

00:37:25.350 --> 00:37:27.580
we just talked about?

00:37:27.580 --> 00:37:36.660
Well, deep learning tries to simulate how
a human brain works, and it has-- the original

00:37:36.660 --> 00:37:40.540
ones were called neural
networks, just like we have neurons.

00:37:40.540 --> 00:37:44.900
So it tries to make its own connections and
then it builds what's called the

00:37:44.900 --> 00:37:51.600
hidden layers, so a deep learning model can
have hundreds of layers.

00:37:51.600 --> 00:37:55.960
And it will assume or try to think about a
problem the same way a human thinks about

00:37:55.960 --> 00:37:59.830
a problem, by connecting
ideas, testing it out, seeing what works.

00:37:59.830 --> 00:38:03.030
If it doesn't work, it goes on and creates
a new hidden model.

00:38:03.030 --> 00:38:07.060
Now that's a
very rudimentary explanation of deep learning.

00:38:07.060 --> 00:38:11.670
I'm happy to go into some of the math after
this or maybe during a

00:38:11.670 --> 00:38:16.670
different session, but that's sort of what
you need to know for now.

00:38:16.670 --> 00:38:22.340
And an important part about deep learning
is that we figured out that things like graphics

00:38:22.340 --> 00:38:27.660
processing units, GPUs,
the same thing that runs video games, is actually

00:38:27.660 --> 00:38:30.560
really good at doing matrix math, and deep
learning tends to

00:38:30.560 --> 00:38:31.980
involve a lot of matrix math.

00:38:31.980 --> 00:38:36.000
So at IBM, we are talking about big data here.

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:41.660
When you need to do deep learning
against large amounts of data or large streams

00:38:41.660 --> 00:38:44.880
of data, you have to use GPUs.

00:38:44.880 --> 00:38:48.790
So that's why cars that are coming
out now that are learning to do image detection

00:38:48.790 --> 00:38:53.870
and find other cars and people on the road
are using GPUs

00:38:53.870 --> 00:38:54.890
onboard.

